   "attributes": null,
   "items": [
    {
     "body": "<p>This refers to encrypted web content that is not indexed by conventional search engines and requires specific software, authorization, or configurations to access. Expert researchers monitor the dark web for new threat intelligence.</p>",
     "title": "The Dark Web",
     "_graphic": {
      "alt": "A hacker icon on a desktop screen",
      "src": "en-US/assets/e66fe7feacf649188ca0ce1fc4b1cd91.png",
      "attribution": ""
     },
     "strapline": "Tap + for more information",
     "_ariaLevel": 0,
     "_index": 0,
     "_parentId": "63ac41b1248b18028273530b"
    },
    {
     "body": "<p>IOCs such as malware signatures or malicious domain names provide evidence of security breaches and details about them.</p>",
     "title": "Indicator of Compromise (IOC)",
     "_graphic": {
      "alt": "A magnifying glass",
      "src": "en-US/assets/7066f66d2d5b4aaab9efc342d4e85566.png",
      "attribution": ""
     },
     "strapline": "Tap + for more information",
     "_ariaLevel": 0,
     "_index": 1,
     "_parentId": "63ac41b1248b18028273530b"
    },
    {
     "body": "<p>Automated Indicator Sharing (AIS), a Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) capability, enables the real-time exchange of cybersecurity threat indicators using a standardized and structured language.&nbsp; Structured Threat Information Expression (STIX) and Trusted Automated Exchange of Intelligence Information (TAXII) are standards&nbsp;used in AIS.</p>",
     "title": "Automated Indicator Sharing (AIS)",
     "_graphic": {
      "alt": "Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency logo",
      "src": "en-US/assets/af4e1bebcdae4ee498d17d49e16f2896.png",
      "attribution": ""
     },
     "strapline": "Tap + for more information",
     "_ariaLevel": 0,
     "_index": 2,
     "_parentId": "63ac41b1248b18028273530b"
    }
   ]
  },
